d crewMember \u2192 familiarizationRecord \u2192 familiarizationRecordItem paths, without adding unjustified minCount constraints; represent the two ship-to-crew relationships so they do not impose duplicate equivalent crew-member obligations."],"current_feedback":"The graph does not enforce the core qualification that every PWOM item relevant to a crew member's assigned duties is covered by that crew member's familiarization record. It independently checks hasRelevantPolarWaterOperationalManualItem and familiarizationRecordItem, so an unrelated record item can satisfy the structure while the relevant duty item is uncovered. Add a bounded SHACL constraint (Core plus one suitable query if needed) that links each assigned-duty relevant item to the corresponding familiarizationRecordItem, while preserving the authoritative ship-owned status, required hasCrewMember and hasCrewMemberInventory paths, and the existing non-existence-enforcing cardinalities.","blocking":false,"semantic_attempt_consumed":false}
